 "title": "How to Become Ridiculously Social",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator shares 5 tips on how to become more social and confident around people. The main lesson is to take small, low-pressure actions like speaking immediately, assuming friendliness, and doing daily social reps to build confidence.",
 "key_points": [
  "Speak immediately by saying hello within 3 seconds of entering a room to avoid overthinking and anxiety.",
  "Assume people already like you and act like you are greeting an old friend so they match your energy.",
  "Use the icebreaker shortcut by giving a specific compliment, such as asking where someone got their jacket.",
  "Seek advice by asking simple questions like 'What should I order?' because people love giving recommendations and feeling helpful.",
  "Do daily reps such as saying thank you to a barista, waving to a neighbor, or making quick eye contact to make big crowds feel less intimidating."
 ],
 "content": "10 out of 10 ways to become ridiculously social. Number one, speak immediately. Say hello within 3 seconds of entering a room. Don't let your brain overthink or build unnecessary anxiety. Number two, assume that they already like you. Assume people are already friendly, act like you're greeting an old friend.. and they'll match your energy. Number three, the icebreaker shortcut. Compliment something specific. For example... \"That jacket is cool, where'd you get it?\" Number four, seek advice. Ask simple questions like \"What should i order?\" People love giving recommendations and feeling helpful. Number five, daily reps. Say \"thank you\" to a barista, wave to a neighbour or make quick eye contact. Small daily reps make big crowds feel less intimidating.\n\nText shown on screen:\n- 10/10 Ways to become Ridiculously Social\n- #fyp #social #teen #motivation #communication\n- 1. Speak immediately\n- Say “hello” within 3 seconds of entering a room.\n- Don't let your brain overthink or build unnecessary anxiety.\n- 2. Assume that they already like you.\n- Assume people are already friendly, act like you're greeting an old friend..\n- and they'll match your energy.\n- 3. The icebreaker shortcut\n- Compliment something specific. For example...\n- “That jacket is cool, where'd you get it?”\n- 4. Seek advice\n- Ask simple questions like “What should i order?”\n- People love giving recommendations and feeling helpful.\n- 5. Daily reps\n- Say “thank you” to a barista, wave to a neighbour or make quick eye contact.\n- Small daily reps make big crowds feel less intimidating.",
